// no-demoted-dialog-confirm — a dialog footer's confirm must outrank its dismiss.
//
// `secondary` is the variant behind the real footers this rule was written
// for: `bg-secondary` sits within roughly 1.1:1 of the dialog surface in both
// themes, and the base class draws `border-transparent`, so the button reads
// as flat text and LOSES the emphasis contest with the `outline` Cancel
// standing beside it. A footer authored that way inverts the visual
// hierarchy: the escape action reads as the primary one and the actual
// primary CTA reads as de-emphasized text.
//
// `ghost`, `link` and `link-muted` are flat at rest too, so the failure shape
// is not unique to `secondary`. They are not plausible footer-confirm choices
// and no such footer exists in the codebase, so the pattern below stays
// narrow rather than widening to catch a shape nobody writes. If one lands,
// widen the pattern rather than assuming it is already covered.
//
// The confirm belongs on `default` (or `destructive` when the action is
// irreversible removal). Both bake `font-mono uppercase` into their variant
// string, so the footer's typographic treatment comes with the variant —
// there is nothing to hand-add. Canonical shape, matching every other
// confirm dialog in the codebase, is to omit the prop entirely and let
// `defaultVariants` supply `default`:
//
//   <DialogFooter>
//     <Button variant="outline" onClick={close}>Cancel</Button>
//     <Button onClick={submit}>Publish</Button>
//   </DialogFooter>
//
// The rule reads the footer element's whole text, so a confirm composed
// indirectly (passed in as a prop, rendered by a shared sub-component) is
// outside its reach. That ceiling is deliberate — it keeps the rule to one
// structural predicate rather than a type-aware analysis.
//
// Suppress a footer that genuinely wants a muted control (a tertiary action
// sitting alongside a properly-weighted confirm) with:
//   // biome-ignore lint/plugin/no-demoted-dialog-confirm: <reason>
//
// See PRECEDENTS.md #42 (custom Biome enforcement is GritQL plugins).

language js

// Matched as one whole element rather than as `<Tag $...>$body</Tag>`,
// because a footer holds two or more children and a single `$body` capture
// binds only an arity-one child list. GritQL regex matches the ENTIRE node
// text, so the leading tag name anchors the match to footers themselves and
// not to any ancestor that happens to contain one. `(?s)` lets `.` cross
// newlines; capturing groups silently never match in Biome's dialect, hence
// `(?:…)`.
jsx_element() as $footer where {
    $footer <: r"(?s)<(?:Alert)?DialogFooter[\s>].*",
    $footer <: r"(?s).*variant=\"secondary\".*",
    register_diagnostic(
        span = $footer,
        message = "Demoted confirm in a dialog footer. `secondary` draws no border and its `bg-secondary` fill sits within about 1.1:1 of the dialog surface, so it reads as flat text and loses the emphasis contest with the `outline` dismiss beside it. Drop the variant prop and let the confirm take `default` (or `destructive` for irreversible removal), which also supplies the footer's font-mono uppercase treatment. See https://github.com/inkeep/open-knowledge/blob/main/biome-plugins/README.md#no-demoted-dialog-confirmgrit"
    )
}
